# Compiled binaries (root only — does not match cmd/headless-macs/ etc.)
/headless-macs
/headless-macs-debug

# go:embed target for headless-macs-debug — built fresh by `make
# debug-binary`/`make build` every time, never committed. A Go build
# isn't byte-reproducible across machines/toolchains even from identical
# source (build-ID hashes, embedded paths), so tracking this as a real
# binary meant every local `make build` permanently conflicted with
# `git pull`. Run `make debug-binary` (or `make build`) once after
# cloning before `go build ./...`/`go vet ./...`/`go test ./...` will
# succeed directly — the same one-time bootstrap step many Go projects
# need for a go:generate output.
/internal/ops/assets/headless-macs-debug

# Go build artifacts
*.test
*.out

